# Feature plans (Kinsenas)

Major feature plans live in **`.cursor/plans/`** in the repo — tracked in git for handoff, same as breakdowns.

Plans are **internal engineering artifacts**. Do not link to `.cursor/plans/` from `docs/admin/` or `docs/members/`.

## When to create a plan file

Create a dated plan in `.cursor/plans/` for:

- New features or multi-file rollouts (before implementation)
- Feature roadmaps and tiered backlogs
- Bug fixes that change behavior across layers (migrations, auth, UI)
- Approved work that will later get a breakdown in `.cursor/breakdowns/`

**Skip a plan file** for lightweight work (copy/styling, single-file tweak, cursor rules only) — use implementation summary only per [plan-implementation.mdc](./plan-implementation.mdc).

## File location and naming

Save to `.cursor/plans/` using this exact pattern (mirrors breakdowns, different suffix):

```
YYYYMMDD-HHMM-<task-slug>-plan.md
```

| Part | Rule |
|------|------|
| `YYYYMMDD` | Local date when the plan is **written** |
| `HHMM` | Local 24-hour time (no colon), e.g. `2112` |
| `<task-slug>` | Short kebab-case label (e.g. `tier-1-improve-existing`, `teams-admin`) |
| Suffix | Always `-plan.md` |

Sort the folder by filename to see the **latest plan first** (newest date/time at top when listed descending).

### Examples

```
.cursor/plans/20260801-2112-feature-roadmap-overview-plan.md
.cursor/plans/20260801-2112-tier-1-improve-existing-plan.md
.cursor/plans/20260815-0930-recurring-obligations-plan.md
```

Compare with breakdowns:

```
.cursor/breakdowns/20260801-0930-disable-email-verification-breakdown.md
```

Same date/time prefix → easy to match a plan to its implementation breakdown.

## Plan content

Follow [feature-planning.mdc](./feature-planning.mdc) for the impact checklist. Every major plan should include, when applicable:

1. Problem / target model
2. Data model & migration
3. Backend — services, requests, policies, props
4. Frontend — types, components, pages
5. Seeders & factories
6. Role / permission / subscription gates
7. Tests — files to update + suggested commands (do not run unless asked)
8. Out of scope

Use YAML frontmatter when helpful:

```yaml
---
name: Short plan title
overview: One-line summary
todos:
  - id: slug
    content: Actionable todo
    status: pending
isProject: true
---
```

## Creating and updating plans

| Rule | Detail |
|------|--------|
| **Create** | New topic → new dated file (do not reuse an old timestamp for a different topic) |
| **Update same topic later** | Append a dated changelog section to the **latest** plan for that `<task-slug>`, or create a new dated plan if scope changed significantly |
| **Multi-tier / roadmap** | One overview plan + one plan per tier or phase, each with its own timestamp |
| **Cross-links** | Link sibling plans with relative paths: `[Tier 1](./20260801-2112-tier-1-improve-existing-plan.md)` |

## Relationship to breakdowns

| Artifact | When | Path pattern |
|----------|------|--------------|
| **Plan** | Before / during design | `.cursor/plans/YYYYMMDD-HHMM-<slug>-plan.md` |
| **Breakdown** | After implementation ships | `.cursor/breakdowns/YYYYMMDD-HHMM-<slug>-breakdown.md` |

Use the same `<task-slug>` when a plan becomes an implementation (e.g. `tier-1-improve-existing`) so pairs are easy to find.

## Agents must not commit unless asked

Creating or editing plans does **not** imply permission to `git commit`. Suggest commit messages only when the user asks.

Suggested commit when plans are added/renamed:

```
Summary: Add dated feature plan(s) for <topic>

<body — what the plan covers and suggested phase order>
```
